cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use clic, please cite it as below."
title: "clic — an open, vendor-neutral compute language"
abstract: >-
  clic is an open, vendor-neutral compute language that keeps CUDA's
  grid-of-threads model without the lock-in. It compiles to Apple Metal today
  and targets FPGA / custom silicon (the OSHI-A1 accelerator) next, with a
  verified library spanning AI (GEMM, attention, softmax, layernorm, RMSNorm,
  conv2d, INT8), hashing (SHA-256), and graphics.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Moriceau
    given-names: Hugo
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-11
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Lastoneparis/clic"
url: "https://github.com/Lastoneparis/clic"
keywords:
  - GPU
  - compiler
  - CUDA alternative
  - AI accelerator
  - inference
  - Metal
  - FPGA
  - RISC-V
  - open source
